<div class="wp-block-group hk-row__text sp-reveal sp-reveal--right"><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"hk-name"} -->
<p class="hk-name">Priya Raman</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"hk-role"} -->
<p class="hk-role">Bakery Shift Lead · Cohort 9</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"hk-body"} -->
<p class="hk-body">Priya Raman supervises production in a busy commercial bakery producing artisan breads, filled morning pastries, and high-protein savory quiches. Before enrolling in Cohort 9, her team logged oven temperatures regularly but lacked a formalized method for checking the core temperature of dairy fillings and cooked meats. Using the digital probe thermometer and calibration methods taught in Week 2, Priya established a mandatory 75 °C core check on all baked savory goods leaving the deck ovens. She also created a dedicated allergen prep bench to prevent cross-contact with tree nuts and sesame seeds. Priya noted that having clear corrective procedures made morning briefings faster and reduced product hold-ups.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>
<!-- /wp:group --></div>
<!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {"className":"hk-row hk-row--rev","layout":{"type":"default"}} -->
