<p class="hk-name">Jonas Weber</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"hk-role"} -->
<p class="hk-role">School-Canteen Cook · Cohort 11</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"hk-body"} -->
<p class="hk-body">Jonas Weber leads the hot meal service at a large school canteen serving several hundred lunches daily within a ninety-minute window. Enrolling in Cohort 11, Jonas sought to overhaul their hot-holding routines and batch cooling records. Through the course lessons on the 5 °C to 63 °C danger zone, Jonas reconfigured the canteen service wells to keep hot-held soups and pasta dishes at a consistent 63 °C or higher right through the second lunch shift. He introduced shallow cooling trays to speed up vegetable stock chilling to 5 °C and trained canteen assistants on two-stage cleaning protocols, creating a calm, predictable daily log routine.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>
<!-- /wp:group --></div>
<!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {"className":"hk-row","layout":{"type":"default"}} -->
